A rehearsal.

Hamlet, a literary/storage device.
Juliet, an orator.
Cleopatra, a storage device for numbers.

                    Act I: The Only Act.

                    Scene I: The Prince's Speech.
[Enter Cleopatra and Hamlet]

Hamlet: Thou art the sum of a lovely sweet warm fine healthy blossoming rose and a king. Speak your mind!

[Exit Cleopatra]

[Enter Juliet]

Juliet: Thou art the sum of Cleopatra and a rose. Speak your mind!

Hamlet: Am I as good as the sum of Cleopatra and a rose?
    If so, speak thy mind!

Juliet: Speak your mind!

[Exeunt]